","Z13.79","Z31.430","Z31.438","Z31.440","Z31.441","Z31.448","Z31.5","Z36.0"]},"asterisked":[],"paragraphs":{"codes":{"1":"Tier 1 Covered Codes Limited coverage may be provided for the genetic tests, submitted under the following CPT codes: Please refer to the Indications and Limitations of Coverage section (L35000) and the ICD-10-CM diagnosis to CPT procedure groupings below.","2":"Tier 1 Individual Review Codes Coverage may be provided for the genetic tests submitted under the following Tier 1 CPT codes, if documentation supports medical necessity: Please refer to the Indications and Limitations of Coverage section (L35000) and the ICD-10-CM diagnosis to CPT procedure groupings below. Not all procedure codes have related diagnosis codes listed.","3":"Tier 1 Non-covered Codes Genetic testing procedures submitted under the following CPT codes are unlikely to impact therapeutic decision-making in the clinical management of the patient and will be denied automatically as not medically necessary:","4":"Tier 2 CPT and NOC Codes Refer to indications and Limitations of Coverage section (L35000). Tier 2/NOC Covered Code/Gene Combinations Limited coverage may be provided for specific genes reported below: 81400 ACE, F13B, F5, F7, FGB 81401 CBFB-MYH11, E2A/PBX1, EML4-ALK, ETV6-RUNX1, EWSR1/ERG, EWSR1/FLI1, EWSR1/WT1, F11coagulation factor XI, FIP1L1-PDGFR, FOXO1/PAX3, FOXO1/PAX7, MUTYH (mutY homolog [E.coli]), NPM/ALK, PAX8/PPARG, RUNX1/RUNX1T1 81403 F8 (coagulation factor VIII), VHL (von Hippel-Lindau tumor suppressor) 81404 CDKN2A (cyclin-dependent kinase inhibitor 2A), PRSS1 (protease, serine, 1 [trypsin 1]), MEN1 (multiple endocrine neoplasia 1) (eg, multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1, Wermer syndrome), duplication/deletion, TP53 (tumor protein 53) (e.g. tumor samples), targeted sequence…","5":"The following PLA codes in Group 5 below are unlikely to impact therapeutic decision-making in the clinical management of the patient and will be denied automatically as not medically necessary:"},"covered":{"1":"CPT codes 81162-81167, 81212, 81215, 81216, 81217 are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","2":"CPT code 81170 is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes","3":"CPT codes 81206, 81207, and 81208 (BCR/ABL) are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","4":"CPT code 81210 (BRAF) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","5":"CPT Code 81218 (CEBPA) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","6":"CPT codes 81315 and 81316 PML/RARALPHA are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","7":"CPT code 81235 (EGFR) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","8":"CPT code 81245, 81246 (FLT3) are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","9":"CPT code 81256 (HFE) is considered medically necessary the following ICD-10-CM codes:","10":"CPT codes 81261-81264 (IGH) are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","11":"CPT codes 81270 (JAK2), 81338 (MPL), 81339 (MPL), 81279 (JAK2 exons 12 and 13), 81219 (CALR), and 0027U (JAK2 exons 12-15) are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes when criteria in Indications and Limitations of Coverage are met:","12":"CPT code 81272 (KIT) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes: CPT code 81273 (KIT) is considered medically necessary only for the diagnosis of mastocytosis.","13":"CPT code 81275 and 81276 (KRAS) are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","14":"CPT code 81287 (MGMT) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","15":"CPT code 81301 Microsatellite instability analysis (e.g., hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer, Lynch syndrome) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","16":"CPT Code 81311 (NRAS) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes","17":"CPT Code 81314 (PDGFRA only) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","18":"CPT code 81332 (SERPINA1) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM code:","19":"CPT codes 81340 (TRB@, PCR), 81341 (TRB@ Southern blot), and 81342 (TRG@) are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","20":"CPT code 81168 CCND1/IGH is considered medically necessary for patients who have non- Hodgkin&rsquo;s lymphoma.","21":"CPT codes 81404 and 81405 (RET- MEN Types 2B (81404) and 2A (81405) are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","22":"CPT code 81406 (ATP7B) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM code:","23":"CPT codes 81518, 81519, 81521, 81522, 81523 (Oncology, breast mRNA) and CPT 81520 Prosigna® Breast Cancer Prognostic Gene Signature Assay are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","24":"CPT code 81595 Cardiology (heart transplant), mRNA is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","25":"CPT code 81310 NPM1 (nucleophosmin) is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","26":"CPT codes 81352 TP53 (tumor protein 53) (e.g. tumor samples), targeted sequence analysis of 2-5 exons, and CPT code 81351 TP53 (tumor protein 53) (e.g. Li-Fraumeni syndrome, tumor samples), full gene sequence or targeted sequence analysis of >5 exons are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes","27":"CPT code 81334 RUNX1 gene is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","28":"CPT codes 81175-81176-ASXL1 gene is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","29":"CPT codes 81120-81121, IDH1 and IDH2, are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes: CPT code 81345, TERT, is considered medically necessary for C71.0-C71.9 only.","30":"CPT code 81305 MYD88 is considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM codes:","31":"CPT code 81261, 81262, 81263, and 81264 (IGH) are considered medically necessary for the following ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes. Please use Modifier 91 as appropriate, based on the Medicare Claims Processing Manual Chapter 16, Laboratory Services Section 100.5.1. Modifier 91 may be is used \"to indicate that a test was performed more than once on the same day for the same patient., only when it is necessary to obtain multiple results in the course of treatment.\""},"noncovered":{"1":"The following ICD-10-CM codes are considered non-covered for all molecular pathology procedures:"}}}]